---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Training diagram"
  title="Create the noisy input and keep the noise as a target"
  caption="Reconstructed from page 44. Sample a data point, a timestep and independent Gaussian noise; obtain xₜ directly from x₀, then predict the sampled noise from xₜ and t. The clean point is used to construct the training input, not supplied separately to the predictor. The loss may retain the interior ELBO weight wₜ or use the simplified unweighted objective; their timestep ranges and scaling differ as described in the text. No training results are plotted."
>
  <svg class="wide" viewBox="0 0 860 395" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-train-wide-title ddpm-train-wide-desc">
    <title id="ddpm-train-wide-title">Noise-prediction training uses a known sampled noise target</title>
    <desc id="ddpm-train-wide-desc">A clean data point x0 and independent Gaussian epsilon enter direct noising with coefficients set by a sampled timestep t. The resulting xt and the timestep enter the noise predictor. Its prediction and the original epsilon are compared by a squared-error loss. Epsilon is both used to construct the noisy input and retained as the supervised target.</desc>
    <defs><marker id="ddpm-train-wide-head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="head" /></marker></defs>
    <g class="input"><rect x="40" y="36" width="180" height="80" rx="4" /><rect x="350" y="36" width="160" height="80" rx="4" /><rect x="650" y="36" width="180" height="80" rx="4" /></g>
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="130" y="67" class="strong">Clean example x₀</text><text x="130" y="94" class="muted">Sample from data</text><text x="430" y="67" class="strong">Timestep t</text><text x="430" y="94" class="muted">Sample uniformly</text><text x="740" y="67" class="strong">Known noise ε</text><text x="740" y="94" class="muted">Draw N(0, I)</text></g>
    <g class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-train-wide-head)"><path d="M 130 116 V 223" /><path d="M 430 116 V 154 H 180 V 223" /><path d="M 430 116 V 223" /><path d="M 740 116 V 192 H 270 V 223" /><path d="M 740 116 V 223" /></g>
    <text x="42" y="174" class="muted">Signal</text><text x="257" y="146" class="muted">Set coefficients</text><text x="445" y="174" class="muted">Condition on t</text><text x="556" y="183" class="muted">Construct corruption</text><text x="750" y="154" class="accent">Keep target</text>
    <g class="node"><rect x="35" y="230" width="270" height="82" rx="4" /><rect x="375" y="230" width="185" height="82" rx="4" /><rect x="645" y="230" width="185" height="82" rx="4" /></g>
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="170" y="258" class="strong">Direct noising</text><text x="170" y="283">xₜ = √ᾱₜ x₀ + √(1−ᾱₜ) ε</text><text x="467" y="258" class="strong">Noise predictor</text><text x="467" y="287">εθ(xₜ, t)</text><text x="737" y="258" class="strong">Squared error</text><text x="737" y="287">‖ε − εθ(xₜ, t)‖²</text></g>
    <g class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-train-wide-head)"><path d="M 312 272 H 368" /><path d="M 567 272 H 638" /></g>
    <text x="339" y="258" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">xₜ</text><text x="603" y="258" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Predict</text>
    <path d="M 35 335 H 830" class="rule" />
    <text x="430" y="365" text-anchor="middle">One sampled noise level per example; no forward rollout is needed.</text>
  </svg>

  <svg class="narrow" viewBox="0 0 320 725" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-train-narrow-title ddpm-train-narrow-desc">
    <title id="ddpm-train-narrow-title">A vertical view of noise-prediction training</title>
    <desc id="ddpm-train-narrow-desc">Sample a timestep, a clean example and independent Gaussian noise. Construct xt directly. Feed xt and the timestep to the predictor. Route the original sampled epsilon separately to the loss as its target, and compare the prediction to that target.</desc>
    <defs><marker id="ddpm-train-narrow-head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="head" /></marker></defs>
    <rect x="40" y="15" width="240" height="59" rx="4" class="input" />
    <text x="160" y="40" text-anchor="middle" class="strong">Sample a timestep t</text><text x="160" y="62" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Sets the corruption level</text>
    <g class="input"><rect x="20" y="108" width="126" height="65" rx="4" /><rect x="174" y="108" width="126" height="65" rx="4" /></g>
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="83" y="134" class="strong">Data x₀</text><text x="83" y="157" class="muted">Clean input</text><text x="237" y="134" class="strong">Noise ε</text><text x="237" y="157" class="muted">Draw N(0, I)</text></g>
    <g class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-train-narrow-head)"><path d="M 83 173 V 202 H 100 V 226" /><path d="M 237 173 V 202 H 220 V 226" /><path d="M 40 44 H 8 V 414 H 37" /></g>
    <text x="160" y="216" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Mix using t</text>
    <rect x="44" y="234" width="232" height="94" rx="4" class="node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="160" y="260" class="strong">Direct noising</text><text x="160" y="289">xₜ = √ᾱₜ x₀</text><text x="160" y="313">+ √(1−ᾱₜ) ε</text></g>
    <path d="M 160 335 V 373" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-train-narrow-head)" /><text x="176" y="361" class="muted">Noisy xₜ</text>
    <rect x="44" y="380" width="232" height="77" rx="4" class="node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="160" y="407" class="strong">Noise predictor</text><text x="160" y="434">εθ(xₜ, t)</text></g>
    <path d="M 160 464 V 523" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-train-narrow-head)" /><text x="175" y="493" class="muted">Prediction</text>
    <path d="M 300 140 H 311 V 558 H 283" class="target" marker-end="url(#ddpm-train-narrow-head)" />
    <rect x="44" y="530" width="232" height="86" rx="4" class="node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="160" y="556" class="strong">Compare with known ε</text><text x="160" y="585">‖ε − εθ(xₜ, t)‖²</text></g>
    <text x="160" y="645" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">The right path keeps ε as the target.</text>
    <text x="160" y="676" text-anchor="middle">One selected noise level;</text><text x="160" y="700" text-anchor="middle">no forward rollout.</text>
  </svg>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px; }
  .strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); font-size: 15px; }
  .input { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .arrow, .head, .target { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.7; stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .target { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .rule { stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  .narrow { display: none; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) {
    .wide { display: none; }
    .narrow { display: block; max-width: 340px; margin-inline: auto; }
  }
</style>
